sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-013: Browse and Filter Open Team Vacancies — Recruitment Board Sequence
    actor User
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant FirebaseAuth
    participant DiscoveryService
    participant PostgreSQL

    User->>ReactUI: Open platform recruitment board and enter filters
    ReactUI->>ReactUI: Validate skills, role, goal, and minimum slots
    alt Client validation fails
        ReactUI-->>User: Field errors with filter values preserved
    else Valid filters
        ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/teams with filters and no eventId
        ExpressAPI->>FirebaseAuth: Classify Visitor or verify token, MFA, active verified PART
        alt Authenticated token is invalid or ineligible
            FirebaseAuth-->>ExpressAPI: 401 or 403 explicit failure
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: No participant projection
            ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: Optional retry without credentials
        else Visitor or verified PART
            FirebaseAuth-->>ExpressAPI: Viewer category
        end
        ExpressAPI->>DiscoveryService: Sanitized combinable filters and viewer category
        DiscoveryService->>PostgreSQL: Read Open teams, Open vacancies, and Confirmed roster counts
        PostgreSQL-->>DiscoveryService: Recruitment records and internal shadow lifecycle metadata
        DiscoveryService->>DiscoveryService: Exclude hidden, locked, disbanded, expired, and slotless records
        DiscoveryService->>DiscoveryService: Match goal, minimum slots, and same-vacancy role plus all skills
        alt Verified PART
            DiscoveryService->>DiscoveryService: Allow-list pitch, member display names and roles, and apply identifiers
        else Visitor
            DiscoveryService->>DiscoveryService: Build anonymized preview without names, pitch, members, links, or identifiers
        end
        DiscoveryService-->>ExpressAPI: At most 50 projected cards and total
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 200 PART cards or VISITOR previews
        alt No matching teams
            ReactUI-->>User: Empty state and Reset Filters action
        else Results available
            ReactUI-->>User: Cards, sign-in prompts, or Apply controls
            User->>ReactUI: Apply to an open slot
            ReactUI-->>User: Open US-018 application form
        end
    end

    Note over DiscoveryService,PostgreSQL: Current filtering still derives mutability from the backend shadow event status and end date. No user selects or submits that internal event.

